# Line endings.
#
# This repo is built and deployed from Linux (GitHub Actions, Vercel builders),
# always from a fresh clone. The LF blob in git is therefore the artifact that
# actually ships. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites tracked
# text to CRLF, so the working copy stops matching the thing that gets built and
# served. That is a defect in the checkout, not in the tests that catch it, and
# both rules below name a concrete mechanism that breaks without them.

# Everything under apps/property-explorer/public is copied into dist and served
# to clients byte for byte, so the committed blob is the served bytes.
#
# "-text" rather than "text eol=lf" on purpose: git performs no end-of-line
# conversion in either direction, which keeps two properties. The blob is
# literally what ships, and the llms.txt contract assertion in
# apps/property-explorer/src/lib/pe-llms-txt.test.ts stays a true byte
# comparison against the LLMS_TXT template literal on every platform. Under
# "text eol=lf" git would silently rewrite a CRLF commit and that assertion
# could never fail on line endings again.
apps/property-explorer/public/** -text

# Shebang scripts must check out with LF.
#
# vite's SSR transform locates the hashbang with /^#!.*\n/ (vite 6.4.3,
# ssrTransformScript). "." does not match "\r" in JavaScript, so on a CRLF file
# the pattern never matches, fileStartIndex falls back to 0, and the hoisted
# __vite_ssr_import__ block is inserted BEFORE the "#!". That leaves a hashbang
# part-way through the source, which is a SyntaxError, and the importing test
# file fails to collect with no useful message.
#
# Nine tracked .mjs files carry a shebang. render-mark.mjs is the one currently
# imported by a vitest suite (apps/property-explorer/scripts/render-mark.test.mjs),
# but the rule is written for the class rather than that one file, because the
# next test to import any of the other eight would hit the identical failure.
*.mjs text eol=lf
